# What `vite build --mode desktop` is building.
#
# The game is one application and this is the only line that says which shape of
# it is being bundled. `desktop` is what tells the browser-only parts of the game
# to stand down — no service worker, no install offer, no update bar
# (`src/platform/target.ts`) — and what tells `src/platform/files.ts` that a
# career file must go through the shell's own writer rather than a download that
# a WebView or a window will not catch.
#
# The default, when this is missing, is `web`: a build that declares nothing is
# the build that already works, so no packaging step can change how the game
# behaves by forgetting to say something. See `.env.native` for the phone's copy
# of this file, and `DESKTOP.md` for what the desktop target changes.
VITE_BUILD_TARGET=desktop
